      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. That is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nI suspect one of these was intended:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day total\n- **2550 mg/day** split some other way, such as 1,000 mg in the morning and 1,000 mg at lunch and 550 mg at dinner. This is unusual.\n- A lower dose, since many patients are titrated to less than the maximum.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If you really do want 2550 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it."
      }
