     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is about three times the maximum labeled dose. Extra metformin adds no glycemic benefit, but it greatly raises the risk of severe lactic acidosis. That risk applies even with normal renal and hepatic function. I can't treat this as a routine order, so I'd rather say that plainly than enter it quietly.\n\nI can enter either of these now:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- A lower dose you prefer, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg BID, or a titration schedule\n\nIf you have a reason for the higher dose, such as a research protocol or a specific toxicology or clinical-pharmacology plan, please discuss it with pharmacy first. Pharmacy can then verify it and document it through the hospital's dose-override process.\n\nTell me which dose to enter and I'll do it right away."
      }
     ],
